WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.280
- Episode 4!
- We're already on Episode 4!

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.720
Let's see what we've
got in this episode.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.120
This show has cute moments, secrets coming
out, drama, and plenty of silliness.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.800
It's got it all,
whatever you're in the mood for.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.160
Want a laugh? Some tension? Or…
something lovey-dovey? We've got it all.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.600
<i>When I met you at Paradise that day,</i>
<i>I thought you were like my mom.</i>

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>Trying to land a rich</i>
<i>partner to improve your life.</i>

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.880
<i>Getting close to me</i>
<i>for money and comfort.</i>

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.837
<i>But after I got to know you</i>
<i>and spent time with you,</i>

00:00:46.837 --> 00:00:50.080
<i>I realized you'd never be like my mom.</i>

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.280
<i>Because money can't buy you.</i>

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.200
<i>Money can buy my time.</i>

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.680
<i>But it can't buy me.</i>

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.080
<i>I'm sorry for everything.</i>

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:32.320
<i>You don't need to apologize.</i>
<i>It's enough that you understand.</i>

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.640
- I love this scene.
- Mm.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.991
- It feels like both characters are…
this is where they first click.

00:01:44.991 --> 00:01:46.840
- Where they open up to each other.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:01.240
For Peem, it's not easy
to talk about this trauma.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:08.400
So I feel like this is another scene
that shows she's starting to let Parn in.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.400
We talked about this before.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.000
- Peem never even planned to tell Parn.
- Mm.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:21.520
But… yeah. Episode 4 is where
she really cracks that shell.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.760
- You get me?
- Mm.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:28.160
We can see another side to them here.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:35.560
The audience gets to understand
Peem better, and Parn too.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:39.160
<i>But I want to pay for you.</i>

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:52.960
<i>I told you… because I wanted</i>
<i>to ask for your permission.</i>

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:02.760
<i>If doing something makes you happy,</i>
<i>you can go ahead and do it.</i>

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.440
Was Parn just thinking on her feet?

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.680
She knew she shouldn't go,
but didn't want Peem to worry even more.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.040
So she said she'd take a baking class.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.640
- Didn't she plan to take it?
- Yes, I mean right when she said it.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.680
I wondered about that and forgot to ask.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:26.360
But when I rewatched it,
I wasn't sure I'd read it right.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:31.475
I think Parn knew she shouldn't
go to work the next day.

00:03:31.475 --> 00:03:36.240
But she wanted to…
make things a little less awkward.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:40.160
- To smooth it over, she'd take it for real.
- Oh.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:43.920
- She saw a chance to…
- That's another way to look at it.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.720
I'm not sure about that.
It depends on how the actor interprets it.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.160
That's my take,
but I can't say for sure.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:55.600
- It felt like Parn was improvising.
- Yeah, that could be another reason.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.880
That's all Peem needs to understand.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.240
- Oh, right.
- Yeah, that's all Peem needs.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.240
Parn smoothed it over
without making Peem feel bad.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:07.840
She knew Peem couldn't say "don't go
to work." So I… I mean, Parn went,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:11.720
"Then can I take a baking class?"
She'd wanted to anyway. Good opportunity.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:15.480
That's the thinking behind the scene.
And we've never discussed it.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:18.200
- <i>Yes, I'll go there myself.</i>
- I like this scene.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.520
- <i>Drive safe, get home early, okay?</i>
- This feels weird. Cringe!

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.176
- <i>Do your best, okay?</i>
- I'm so short here.

00:04:24.176 --> 00:04:25.280
- This is cringey.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.273
Even the characters seemed
embarrassed by what they were saying.

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:33.880
Like, "What did I just say?"

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.746
- Is that where Peem goes all sweet on Parn?

00:04:37.746 --> 00:04:41.160
- Yeah. See?
She's out here grumbling. "Okay?"

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.101
I think she's so in love that she
manages to get those words out.

00:04:50.101 --> 00:04:52.280
But she still cringes at herself anyway.

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:54.000
Like, "What did I just say?"

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.680
They still don't know
each other that well.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.200
When Peem said that,
let's say Parn felt good.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.840
But it didn't surprise her yet.
Not at that point.

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:07.320
She hadn't seen… enough of
Peem's cold side to be surprised.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.040
More like, "Oh,
she has that side to her too?"

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.200
<i>I want you near me day and night.</i>

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.480
Is this the love scene you like?

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.600
Yeah. I think this love
scene is done well.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.945
- A 360…
- Panoramic.

00:05:35.945 --> 00:05:37.760
- A 360-degree view.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:41.367
- It was our first love scene.
It wasn't easy.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.367
- Mm.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.640
That is so revealing!

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:17.080
Good thing Mol called, though.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.685
- It was Parn's phone,
the one she left with Mol.

00:06:21.685 --> 00:06:22.685
- Oh.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.880
Ooh, that startled me.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:45.000
<i>Ms. Peem. You just won't let it end and</i>
<i>have to do this behind my back, huh?!</i>

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:02.000
<i>Thank you for loving me.</i>

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.600
<i>But next time,</i>
<i>don't sacrifice so much for me.</i>

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.240
This song's in almost every love scene.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:27.040
No, this is the one they play when…
the love scene is on the softer side.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.160
When it's steamy, there's another song.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.200
But I love this one. It's iconic.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.760
- The lyrics are touching.
- Mm.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.000
- We didn't swallow any.
- No, we didn't.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:00.720
Everyone took really
good care of us that day.

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:04.720
No. I just added more bubbles to my
back to make the tub look fuller.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:09.120
I don't think any got in our mouths.
Just a big blob on my neck.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:10.840
Oh, like when we…

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:16.120
- No, I don't remember swallowing any soap.
- Nope, we didn't swallow any bubbles!

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.240
I love the kneeling scene. No doubt.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.320
- Yeah, it hits hard.
- Since I read the script,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.800
I knew this scene would be… I cried
when I read it. The tears just came.

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:27.960
I love it.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:34.200
It's another scene that shows how much
Peem loves Parn. That's why I love it.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:38.205
- She gets down on her knees in
front of Songsak, a guy who's…

00:08:38.205 --> 00:08:40.800
- Her business rival.
- Right. It's just…

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:45.280
It's beyond anything
you'd expect from Peem.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.200
Yeah. I really love that scene.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.600
What I really loved
about this episode was…

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:54.960
There's a scene where they talk on
the balcony outside Peem's office.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.360
That scene really stuck with me.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.040
Peem doesn't open up easily.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:07.480
But she chose to tell Parn what hurt her.
That's when she really let Parn in.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.080
Oh, the part about her mom?

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:12.160
It's a really sensitive
subject for Peem.

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:20.400
It's the one trauma that
made her who she is.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.120
That scene moved me.
She lets Parn in. You can feel it.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.920
Yeah, she sees me as…
she sees Parn as a person.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.480
She sees that I'm more
than just an object.

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.520
She sees I have a life of my own.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.200
She sees someone she
wants to take care of.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:39.320
It's not just, "Ooh, go for it!"

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:45.847
Another episode where we see what
both characters would give up,

00:09:45.847 --> 00:09:49.200
and how far they'll go for each other.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.800
All of this sets up
the drama in Episode 5.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.920
Yep. Episode 5 goes boom!

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.000
- Mm.
- So much love, so much hurt.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.640
- The deeper the love, the more it hurts.
- That's true.

